course: dictionary
lesson: 13319
title: Words for people at work
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Many words name a job. You can work out a job word from the words around it. «The groundsman cut the grass on the football pitch.» Cutting grass and a football pitch are the clues, so a groundsman looks after a field.
explain: Read the whole sentence before you guess. «The groundsman painted white lines on the school field.» Painting lines on a field is a clue that a groundsman marks out the field for games.
explain: In the USA, the same job is often called a groundskeeper. If you read an American text and meet that word, the context will show you it means the same kind of job.
fact: A groundsman is a person whose job is to look after a sports field, park or school grounds.
fact: A groundsman cuts the grass, marks the lines and takes care of the pitch.
fact: «The groundsman prepared the cricket pitch before the match.» Cricket groundsmen prepare the pitch for the game.
fact: In the USA, a similar job is called a groundskeeper.
exercise: «The groundsman cut the grass on the football pitch.» What does a groundsman do? | *Looks after a sports field by cutting grass and marking lines | Sells tickets at the football match | Teaches maths in a primary school | Drives the school bus
exercise: «The groundsman painted white lines on the school field.» Find and copy the word that names a job. | lines | field | *groundsman | painted
exercise: In the USA, a similar job is called a groundskeeper. What is a groundsman called in the USA? | Referee | Umpire | *Groundskeeper | Lollipop lady
test: «The cricket groundsman prepared the pitch before the game.» What does a cricket groundsman prepare? | The bus timetable | The school dinners | The library books | *The pitch
test: «The groundsman mows the playing fields every week.» Where does a groundsman work? | *A sports field or school grounds | A post office counter | A bakery shop | A hospital ward
exam: What is the job of a groundsman? | Writing the school newsletter | Driving a train to the station | *Looking after a park, sports field or school grounds | Serving food in a school canteen
